Hey everyone!

In todays update we introduce a feature that was highly requested by the community! Controls! You can now change controls to better match your playstyle. This, aswell as some adjustements made to the car system and optimizations.

Update 0.5 contains the following changes:

- Optimized loot system for performance;
- Fixed a bug where loot would reroll after you closed the menu;
- Optimized audio files for faster scene loading times;
- Introduced a controls menu! - players can now change controls to their liking;
- Fixed all of the game's labels to match the correct labels of the actions done;
- Introduced a black outline for all the labels on the bottom of the screen for better visibility in bright areas;
- Reduced the overall damage the car takes from all hits;
- Improved overall detection of car hits;

Next big update, we plan to implement a translation system into the game aswell as a new system for the car which includes overall better control and handling. 
We're working on a new vegetation system which includes biomes, this will have a significant impact on the maps overall look and performance so it will take a bit more time to make perfect, in the upcoming week we will release some screenshots to show you the progress on that to keep you updated!

Thank you everyone who has stuck by us on this journey, the game is only getting better and we are happy to see everyone is enjoying it!

Hey everyone!

Today we have a biiiiiig update for you guys! Lots of bug fixes, adjustments and a full overhaul to the sprinting system are in place!

The changes for Update 0.4 are:

- Fixed a bug where blockers were not in place for one of the factorys buildings;
- Corrected the Shaperned Stone crafting recipe description;
- Crafting a gauze should now give you the correct item;
- Crafting an Heavy Bandage should now give you the correct item;
- Level is now displayed correctly when starting the game or loading a last save;
- Closing the sleep menu on a bed or sleeping bag now awakes you automatically;
- UI on the sleeping bag no longer rotates with the object;
- Sleep speed rate normalized on beds;
- You should now be able to sleep on all beds in the game;
- Fixed a bug where the player wasnt colliding with the bed;
- Prevented players from going up ladders in the Military Base;
- Removed ability to rotate the trident trap (due to a bug that was happening with the UI);
- Adjusted jump values;
- Corrected the Unstuck label;
- The character should now never attack when a UI window is open and you click anywhere on the screen;
- Fixed a bug where the character stopped being able to attack after the player closed an UI window;
- Fixed a bug where you could control a progress bar when doing an action;
- Improved load times;
- Added loot to all cars in the game;
- Fixed Shotgun reloading adding more bullets than it was supposed to;


[b]- Sprint system overhaul:[/b]

  - Sprinting is now directional, you can sprint facing enemies!
  - The character no longer locks in the sprinting animation;
  - You are now able to melee attack while sprinting;
  - Fixed a bug where the character would sprint faster or slower if you hovered over an UI element while sprinting;

Thank you to everyone reporting bugs! We are hard at work fixing the game more and more everyday! Hope you guys enjoy the update!

Hey everyone!

Todays update is a big one! We finally fixed major bugs with the inventory system and stabilized it. Along with that we fixed more bugs, made corrections and added some new features!
Update 0.3 is a big one, so bare with us on this one! :smiley:
Here are the changes:

- Fixed Empty gas can crafting recipe description;
- Fixed Medical kit crafting recipe description;
- Fixed Stone Pickaxe, Hammer crafting recipe descripition;
- Fixed bandits not engaging in combat;
- Bandit onslaught should now be better represented (More bandits spawn);
- Bandits now roam areas after finishing the bandit onslaught quest;
- Inventory huge Stability update;
- .9mm, 45mm and 51mm bullet boxes removed;
- Added sound recognition to all AI. All enemies should now aggro when hearing footsteps or bullet noise;
- Zombies will now wander when spawned. They should only aggro when they hear or see the player;
- Added global bullet impact effects;
- Added ability to unstack items by pressing SHIFT + Right Mouse button on 
 a stacked item and dragging it to another slot. You will be prompted to choose how many items you want to unstack and confirm;
- Bandits can now damage the car;
- You can now run over bandits;
- Added metal scraps to all loots;
- Fixed having to use a lockpick on the locked house after you've completed the mission and already unlocked it;
- Fixed a bug where if you picked up the shotgun in the locked house, all the bullets would despawn;
- Changed current magazine recipes to be crafted with gunpowder instead of bullet boxes;
- Fixed dialog with the survivor in the suburbs;
- Energy bars and Energy drinks now stack up to 5;
- Increased stack size of cooked meat and fish to 5;
- Added back time scale increase when sleeping;
- Fixed time going faster and faster the more times you clicked on the sleep button;

Huge thank you to everyone reporting bugs, giving feedback and suggestions for the game to grow! We are committed and will make this game fulfill its potential!

Hey everyone!

As requested by the community, with todays update a pause system was put in place so players have a chance to pause whenever they want. Along with that we made additional fixes.

The changes for Update 0.2 are as follows:

- Added a pause system, when you pause the game using the Escape key, it now correctly pauses the game;
- Save button now hidden while the character is sleeping (This change is in place so the player more accurately controls the time in which they save the game);
- Fixed Suburbs survivor dialog not showing up;
- Temporarily removed all autosaves in certain quests that were causing a bug to happen where the player couldnt progress further (This will later be reintroduced);
- Reduced the sleeping bag crafting recipe requirements to 2x Cloths;
- Reduced the Empty Gas Can crafting recipe requirements to 2x Plastic Pieces;
- Fixed a bug where you could use consumables infinitely;
- Added an additional tip to help players save the game;
- Fixed a bug where you couldnt reload the shotgun after picking it up in the suburbs;
- Fixed a bug where, after picking up a shotgun from the ground, the quest system would break;
- Fixed the scrollbar in the crafting menu so it better represents how many items are in the crafting list;

Thank you to everyone who reported bugs and gave some feedback about the game!

Hey everyone! 

Following bug reports and feedback from people, we decided to tune the first part of the game and re-adjust some values in order to make it easier for newer players of V1RUZ. With that, we tweaked the Stamina system as we feel it helps the gameplay in a major way, makes the game flow better and reduces downtime. 
Here are the changes for Update 0.1:

- Reduced hunger drain values over time by 30%;
- Reduced thirst drain values over time by 30%;
- Reduced energy usage values over time by 30%;
- Reduced sleep drain values over time by 30%;
- Fixed a bug which caused the hotbar and all of your chest items to disappear; (Thank you @3231 !!!)
- Reduced the campfire crafting recipe requirements to 3x Rocks and 5x Wooden Sticks;
- Reduced the Trident trap crafting recipe requirements to 5x Wooden Sticks
- Added some rocks manually to the first zone of the game;

[b]Stamina system tweaks:[/b]
         - Reduced the stamina cost for using all weapons by 50%;
         - Reduced running stamina cost by 50%;

Thank you to everyone who has reported bugs and gave feedback about the game!

Hey everyone!

Today we rolled out an hotfix to fix some bugs found by the community! 
Hotfix 1.0.1 contains the following changes:

- Fixed the Gun Repair Kit description;
- Fixed a bug in the "Finding the Motel" mission where, if you quit the game while on that mission, the area block would still be there and you could proceed;
- Fixed a bug where if you died on the second floor of a house and loaded the game, the roof would become visible;
- Adjusted the "Finding extra supplies" mission, so more loot spawns in the suburbs when you get that mission;
- Adjusted the time to respawn of all the loot locations from 5-7 days to 3-5 days;
- Fixed a bug where, when you loaded a game, you would lose everything inside your chests and hotbar;
- Fixed the "Empty Gas can" crafting recipe;
- Fixed a bug where your Gas can would destroy itself when using it;
- Fixed the Stamina stat, upgrading stamina should now correctly increase your stamina;
- Fixed a typo in the "Sharpened Stone" item description;

Thank you to everyone who has been playing and reporting bugs, this helps us alot and is instrumental for the development of this game!

Hey guys,

Today we rolled out an hotfix to fix some of the errors and bugs encountered by players
Hotfix 0.0.1 contains the following changes:

- Improved rabbit AI, they now function correctly and are able to be caught more effectively;
- After you catch a rabbit and strip the meat from it, both the rabbit and the trap despawn;
- Added 4 cloth materials to the chest present in the shed;
- Adjusted the number of cloths you need to craft the sleeping bag;
- Increased the duration of the day (Days should be longer than nights now);
- Added an highlight to the gas station generator.
- Increased the highlighting distance of rocks and sticks

Thank you for all your suggestion and bug reports!
